      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Benadryl is the only thing that will actually stop the histamine reaction, but if you're truly afraid of the drowsiness, you can try taking a single dose of an antihistamine with a fast-acting decongestant instead.\nYour idea of pumping blood to clear the system is dangerous; increased circulation will only spread the allergen and make the swelling worse.\nThat trace amount is not \"dust\" to be ignored, and forcing a workout while your body is reacting to an allergen can lead to severe anaphylaxis.\nStop the session immediately, sit down, and take the medication you need to feel safe.",
